Step 1:
    creating deployment.yml file with nginx latest image

apiVersion: apps/v1       # API version used for Deployments
kind: Deployment         # Resource type is Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx-deployment  # Name of the deployment
spec:
  replicas: 2            # Number of Pod replicas (2 Pods will run)
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx         # Deployment will manage Pods with this label
  template:              # Pod template (what each replica will look like)
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx       # Pods will have this label
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:latest   # Container image to use
          ports:
            - containerPort: 80  # Expose port 80 inside the container


Step 2:
    Now deployment the kubectl apply -f "file name"

Step 3:
     Now verify image version nginx with help kubctl describe deployments.apps "deployment name"
 Labels:  app=nginx
  Containers:
   nginx:
    Image:        nginx:latest
    Port:         80/TCP
    Host Port:    0/TCP


Step 4:
     Scale up the pods with this command "kubectl scale deployment nginx-deployment --replicas=6" 

